O(1) in-use byte counter for dlmalloc. mallinfo().uordblks walks every chunk under the malloc lock (and can spin
forever on a corrupt chunk), so a page's memory monitor could not poll it. dlmalloc now keeps the bytes of its in-use
chunks (chunk sizes, headers included) at the public entry points -- dlmalloc, dlfree, the in-place paths of dlrealloc
and dlrealloc_in_place (the moving path is dlmalloc + dlfree), internal_memalign's returned leader/trailer and
internal_bulk_free (a merged run uncounted once, when disposed) -- with one relaxed atomic each; size_t emscripten_dlmalloc_inuse(void) reads it. ialloc carves one
counted chunk into pieces that dlfree uncounts one by one, so it needs nothing. The mspace_* copies are untouched
(MSPACES is 0 in emscripten). Checked: equals mallinfo().uordblks exactly through 400k random calls of every instrumented entry point.
Rebuild: embuilder build --force libdlmalloc*.

Ported to emscripten 6.0.2 (fna-6.0.2 cc2c139); paths are emscripten 6's src/lib/lib*.js.

diff --git a/system/lib/dlmalloc.c b/system/lib/dlmalloc.c
index 684212f..d6e69a1 100644
--- a/system/lib/dlmalloc.c
+++ b/system/lib/dlmalloc.c
@@ -42,6 +42,19 @@ _Static_assert(MALLOC_ALIGNMENT == 8, "max_align_t must be 8");
 
 #endif // __EMSCRIPTEN__
 
+#if __EMSCRIPTEN__
+/* XXX Emscripten XXX (ikvmcraft emsdk.10.patch): bytes in in-use chunks (chunk sizes, headers included), kept at the
+   public entry points with one relaxed atomic each, so a memory monitor can read the live total in O(1).
+   mallinfo().uordblks gives the same number by walking every chunk under the malloc lock. */
+static size_t dl_inuse_bytes;
+#define DL_INUSE_ADD(n) __atomic_fetch_add(&dl_inuse_bytes, (size_t)(n), __ATOMIC_RELAXED)
+#define DL_INUSE_SUB(n) __atomic_fetch_sub(&dl_inuse_bytes, (size_t)(n), __ATOMIC_RELAXED)
+size_t emscripten_dlmalloc_inuse(void) { return __atomic_load_n(&dl_inuse_bytes, __ATOMIC_RELAXED); }
+#else
+#define DL_INUSE_ADD(n) ((void)0)
+#define DL_INUSE_SUB(n) ((void)0)
+#endif
+
 
 #define __THROW
 #define __attribute_malloc__
